```
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Round Robin Router</title>
  <script>
    // Initialize the counter and the URLs
    let counter = 0;
    const urls = [
      'https://example.com/api/endpoint1',
      'https://example.com/api/endpoint2',
      'https://example.com/api/endpoint3',
      'https://example.com/api/endpoint4',
      'https://example.com/api/endpoint5',
      'https://example.com/api/endpoint6',
      'https://example.com/api/endpoint7',
      'https://example.com/api/endpoint8',
      'https://example.com/api/endpoint9',
      'https://example.com/api/endpoint10'
    ];

    // Function to get the next URL in the round-robin sequence
    function getNextUrl() {
      counter = (counter + 1) % urls.length;
      return urls[counter];
    }

    // Function to make the GET request to the next URL
    function makeRequest() {
      constnextUrl = getNextUrl();
      fetch(nextUrl)
        .then(response => response.json())
        .then(data => console.log(data))
        .catch(error => console.error(error));
    }

    // Call the makeRequest function every 5 seconds
    setInterval(makeRequest, 5000);

    // Also call the makeRequest function initially
    makeRequest();

  </script>
</head>
<body>
</body>
</html>
```
Here's how the code works:

1. We define an array `urls` containing the 10 different fixed URLs.
2. We initialize a `counter` variable to keep track of the current position in the round-robin sequence.
3. The `getNextUrl()` function returns the next URL in the sequence by incrementing the `counter` and taking the modulo of the length of the `urls` array. This ensures that we wrap around to the beginning of the sequence when we reach the end.
4. The `makeRequest()` function makes a GET request to the next URL returned by `getNextUrl()`. It uses the `fetch` API to make the request and logs the response data to the console.
5. We use `setInterval()` to call the `makeRequest()` function every 5 seconds.
6. We also call the `makeRequest()` function initially, so that the first request is made immediately after the page loads.

